# 6. Git and GitHub Commands

| Command                   | Purpose                   |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| git init                  | Initialize Git repository |
| git add .                 | Add all files             |
| git commit -m "message"   | Save project changes      |
| git branch -M main        | Rename branch             |
| git remote add origin URL | Connect GitHub repository |
| git push -u origin main   | Push project to GitHub    |
| git pull origin main      | Pull updates              |
| git status                | Check repository status   |
| git remote -v             | View remote repositories  |
| git clone URL             | Clone repository          |

---

# 7. Installation Process

## Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
```

## Step 2: Open Project Folder

```bash
cd project-folder
```

## Step 3: Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

## Step 4: Run Development Server

```bash
npm run dev
```

---

# 8. Project Initialization

Initialize Git inside the project folder.

## Command

```bash
git init
```

## Purpose

Creates a `.git` folder for version control.

---

# 9. Adding Project Files

Add all project files and folders.

## Command

```bash
git add .
```

## Purpose

Tracks all project files recursively.

---

# 10. Commiting Project

Save project snapshot.

## Command

```bash
git commit -m "Initial project commit"
```

## Purpose

Stores project changes with a commit message.

---

# 11. Connecting GitHub Repository

Connect local project to GitHub.

## Command

```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
```

## Example

```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/150chriss/project.git
```

---

# 12. Pushing Project to GitHub

Upload project files to GitHub.

## Commands

```bash
git branch -M main
```

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

## Purpose

Pushes project files to GitHub repository.

---

# 13. Pulling Project from GitHub

Download updates from GitHub.

## Command

```bash
git pull origin main
```

## Purpose

Updates local repository with remote changes.

---

# 14. Updating Existing Project

After editing files:

## Add Changes

```bash
git add .
```

## Commit Changes

```bash
git commit -m "Updated project"
```

## Push Changes

```bash
git push
```

---

# 15. Cloning Repository

Clone project from GitHub.

## Command

```bash
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
```

---

# 16. .gitignore File

Create `.gitignore` to exclude unnecessary files.

## Example

```text
node_modules/
.env
build/
dist/
vendor/
```

---

# 17. Advantages of Git and GitHub

* Project backup
* Collaboration
* Version tracking
* Easy deployment
* Open-source contribution
* Secure repository hosting

---

# 18. Conclusion

The project successfully demonstrates how modern frontend applications can be developed using React, Vite, and TailwindCSS while managing project versions using Git and GitHub.

Git and GitHub provide professional tools for tracking project changes, collaboration, repository hosting, and deployment.

The project structure is organized professionally and can be extended in the future by integrating backend services and databases.

